# The DCE-MRI run serving the demo is the exception to "no artefacts in git": its
# checkpoint and metrics ARE versioned, so `git clone` + `pip install` is enough to
# replay the demo on another machine. Everything else in the folder stays out.
results_mri_p2_negfix/*
!results_mri_p2_negfix/unet_best.pt
!results_mri_p2_negfix/segmentation_metrics.csv
!results_mri_p2_negfix/segmentation_test_metrics.csv
!results_mri_p2_negfix/eval_report.json
!results_mri_p2_negfix/eval_per_patient.csv

# Slice classifier (imaging.sliceclf): the checkpoint is 2.4 MB and its metrics are
# the evidence behind the localisation claims, so both are versioned.
results_sliceclf/*
!results_sliceclf/sliceclf_best.pt
!results_sliceclf/sliceclf_metrics.csv
!results_sliceclf/sliceclf_test_metrics.json

# demo_cases/ is versioned too: since make_demo_case is slim by default, each case
# is one slice (~0.2 MB), not a 30 MB volume. It carries a single pinned axial slice
# of a public, already de-identified TCIA study (Duke-Breast-Cancer-MRI), so there
# is no PHI to leak -- see scripts/make_demo_cases.py to rebuild them.
